<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE topic
  PUBLIC "-//OASIS//DTD DITA Topic//EN" "topic.dtd">
<topic id="scope-decision-table">
    <title>Scope decision table</title>
    <body>
      <table colsep="1" rowsep="1" frame="all">
      <tgroup cols="3">
        <colspec colname="col1"/>
        <colspec colname="col2"/>
        <colspec colname="col3"/>
        <thead>
          <row>
            <entry>Condition</entry>
            <entry>In scope?</entry>
            <entry>What to do</entry>
          </row>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <row>
            <entry>Entry-level desktop FDM printer</entry>
            <entry>Yes</entry>
            <entry>Continue with this troubleshooting path.</entry>
          </row>
          <row>
            <entry>Flat heated build plate</entry>
            <entry>Yes</entry>
            <entry>Continue with this troubleshooting path.</entry>
          </row>
          <row>
            <entry>PLA filament</entry>
            <entry>Yes</entry>
            <entry>Continue with this troubleshooting path.</entry>
          </row>
          <row>
            <entry>Print starts normally but develops edge lifting or minor warping during
              printing</entry>
            <entry>Yes</entry>
            <entry>Continue with this troubleshooting path.</entry>
          </row>
          <row>
            <entry>Non-PLA material</entry>
            <entry>No</entry>
            <entry>Use a material-specific guide instead.</entry>
          </row>
          <row>
            <entry>Resin printer</entry>
            <entry>No</entry>
            <entry>Use a printer-specific guide instead.</entry>
          </row>
          <row>
            <entry>Printer without a heated build plate</entry>
            <entry>No</entry>
            <entry>Use a guide that matches that hardware setup.</entry>
          </row>
          <row>
            <entry>Printer cannot maintain normal nozzle or build plate temperature</entry>
            <entry>No</entry>
            <entry>Stop this path and use a hardware-specific guide.</entry>
          </row>
          <row>
            <entry>Filament does not extrude normally</entry>
            <entry>No</entry>
            <entry>Stop this path and use a hardware-specific guide.</entry>
          </row>
          <row>
            <entry>Build plate is visibly damaged or unstable</entry>
            <entry>No</entry>
            <entry>Stop this path and use a hardware-specific guide.</entry>
          </row>
          <row>
            <entry>Printer shows clear mechanical looseness, assembly problems, or repeated
              hardware-related instability</entry>
            <entry>No</entry>
            <entry>Stop this path and use a hardware-specific guide.</entry>
          </row>
        </tbody>
      </tgroup>
    </table>
      <p>If manufacturer documentation conflicts with this troubleshooting guidance, follow the manufacturer documentation.</p>
    </body>
  </topic>